SUMMARY:The Moors
LOCATION:UMass Amherst\, 151 Presidents Drive\, Amherst\, MA 01003
DESCRIPTION:Curtain Theater\nA hapless governess\, a mysterious hero\, sche
 ming siblings\, and the bleak setting of the windswept countryside: Jen Si
 lverman’s The Moors has all the trapping of the best gothic yarns writte
 n by folks like the Brontë sisters. At once satire and homage to this sou
 rce material\, this dark and funny play also introduces us to two surprisi
 ngly literate animals and their star-crossed love. This richly weird set-u
 p offers a unique lens to explore the things that motivate us: love\, powe
 r\, the search for connection.\nhttps://events.umass.edu/event/the-moors\n
 From Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://events.umass.edu/event/the-moors
END:VEVENT
