SUMMARY:Albany Berkshire Ballet Presents: The Nutcracker
LOCATION:Colonial Theatre\, 111 South St\, Pittsfield\, MA 01201
DESCRIPTION:Times: 2pm\, 6pm\nCelebrate the magic of the holiday season as 
 Albany Berkshire Ballet (ABB) returns with its annual tour of The Nutcrack
 er. Choreographed by ABB’s Artistic Director Madeline Cantarella Culpo\,
  this beloved production features lavish sets and scenery by Stockbridge n
 ative and renowned theatre and film set designer Carl Sprague\, with costu
 mes by Sam Meredith. Young local dance students join professional ABB danc
 ers in special children’s roles\, sharing the stage with a company of pe
 rformers from across the United States and around the world.\nhttps://www.
 berkshiretheatregroup.org/event/albany-berkshire-ballet-presents-the-nutcr
 acker/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.berkshiretheatregroup.org/event/albany-berkshire-ballet-pre
 sents-the-nutcracker/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2c285d6a855df8974fd42e2f22c3987cd4a3ee65@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART:20261205T210000Z
DTEND:20261205T230000Z
SUMMARY:Haley Kean - Passive Forms
LOCATION:CitySpace\, 43 Main St\, Easthampton\, MA 01027
DESCRIPTION:Art Walk Easthampton\nDecember 5\, 2026 - December 23\, 2026 Ar
 t Walk and Artist reception: Saturday\, December 5\, 4-7pm Exhibition Stat
 ement: In Passive Forms\, I explore the relationship between my hometown o
 f Newtown CT\, and the abandoned institution of Fairfield Hills. Drawing i
 nspiration from Hokusai’s 36 Views of Mount Fuji Series\, I created this
  body of work to illuminate the location that the people of Newtown live t
 heir daily lives around. The campus has been collectively reimagined as an
  active participant in the social ecology of Newtown\; It has become a way
 finding device\, a projection of self and community. In my work\, I interp
 ret space within Fairfield Hills\, while emulating the visceral atmosphere
  of a place with layered identity. I do so through scale and detail within
  the etchings\, juxtaposed with the spontaneous materiality of the plaster
 -casting process. I focus the project with large scale drawings that becom
 e abstracted vignettes of place and time on the site of Fairfield Hills.\n
 https://www.cityspaceeasthampton.org/all-events/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mas
 s: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.cityspaceeasthampton.org/all-events/
END:VEVENT
