UID:6dfcd8a5f3475ca63cb0a8a3859767011da1e096@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART:20261209T223000Z
DTEND:20261210T003000Z
SUMMARY:Art Talk: Amy Beecher on Glotech Cantata
LOCATION:Brattleboro Museum & Art Center\, 10 Vernon St\, Brattleboro\, VT 
 05301
DESCRIPTION:Amy Beecher discusses Glotech Cantata—a performance of moveme
 nt\, sound\, and still images that interprets the dance between women and 
 influencer marketing. Taking the Glotech LED facial mask as its motif\, th
 e work meditates upon our era of aspirational social media\, where women a
 re both the authors and the objects of images. This site-responsive perfor
 mance uses “paintings”—large printed panels of still lifes\, masks\,
  and color abstractions—as both props and a movable set that frame\, con
 ceal\, and cast color onto dancers\, who pit improvised movements against 
 stylized gestures and words.\nhttps://www.brattleboromuseum.org/event/art-
 talk-amy-beecher-on-glotech-cantata/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://p
 ushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.brattleboromuseum.org/event/art-talk-amy-beecher-on-glotech
 -cantata/
END:VEVENT
